  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieved 0.485 acc, and config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) improved to 0.527 acc / 0.510 F1, confirming that adding image features with concat fusion is beneficial. However, we have zero evidence on whether multiprofile aggregation provides additional value over singleprofile. This is a major architectural axis that, if positive, could unlock a whole family of higher-performing configs. Config_018 directly extends the current best (config_016) by switching to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation while holding all other factors constant (pca_n2000, resnet50, concat), making it a clean ablation of the profile/aggregation decision. Avgpool is chosen over transformer because it is simpler, reducing confounding: if multiprofile+avgpool does not help, we can rule out the profile axis cheaply; if it does, we can then test whether transformer aggregation adds further gain. This is the highest-information experiment under the limited budget because it resolves a binary architectural question that gates many downstream decisions."
}

